# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Excess ETH send to pay for gas when deploying a new interchain token is not refunded to caller.
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L327

## Proof of Concept
Consider the following scenario
1. Alice wants to deploy a new interchain Token so she calls InterchainTokenService.deployInterchainToken() with the appropriate args. Now she sent a gasValue of 0.1 ether ( using this for the sake of our scenario).
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-08-axelar-network/blob/69c4f2c3fcefb1b8eb2129af9c3685a44ae5b6fe/interchain-token-service/contracts/InterchainTokenService.sol#L334
2. Token gets deployed and consume less than 0.1 ether
3. Remaining ether is not refunded to Alice.
4. Alice funds have been effectively locked inside the contract

```solidity
function deployInterchainToken(
        bytes32 salt,
        string calldata destinationChain,
        string memory name,
        string memory symbol,
        uint8 decimals,
        bytes memory minter,
        uint256 gasValue
    ) external payable whenNotPaused returns (bytes32 tokenId) {
        address deployer = msg.sender;

        if (deployer == interchainTokenFactory) deployer = TOKEN_FACTORY_DEPLOYER;

        tokenId = interchainTokenId(deployer, salt);

        if (bytes(destinationChain).length == 0) {
            address tokenAddress = _deployInterchainToken(tokenId, minter, name, symbol, decimals);

            _deployTokenManager(tokenId, TokenManagerType.NATIVE_INTERCHAIN_TOKEN, abi.encode(minter, tokenAddress));
        } else {
            _deployRemoteInterchainToken(tokenId, name, symbol, decimals, minter, destinationChain, gasValue);
        }
    }
```

## Tools Used
Manual review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Refund remaining gasValue after token deployment to the caller.


