Metadata are defined as optional in the [`ERC-20`](https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20#name) standards. Additionally, some tokens such as [`MKR`](https://etherscan.io/address/0x9f8f72aa9304c8b593d555f12ef6589cc3a579a2#readContract) do not follow the standard and return their `name` and `symbol` as a `bytes32` instead of a `string`. 

The current implementation would revert and prevent such `ERC-20` tokens from being bridged. Moreover, tokens with empty `symbol` and `name` are permitted to bridge, but the deployment of tokens in the `InterchainTokenFactory` contract would fail on the other side of the bridge and the message would have to be recalled.


