                        msg: msg.clone(),
                        status: MessageStatus::Executed,
                    },
                )
                .map_err(Error::from)?;

            Ok(msg)
        }
    ...
}
```

As we can see, the message status is updated to `Executed` and persistent the status in the storage. But if anything wrong after the message status updated, such that `config.chain_name != msg.destination_chain`, which the `msg` is passed by the users, the message status can't be reverted to previous status. You can also see the the detail [here](https://docs.scrt.network/secret-network-documentation/development/development-concepts/secret-contract-fundamentals/secret-contract-cosmwasm-framework/contract-components/storage):

```md
A commonly used wrapper function to save data is the following. This function overwrites previously saved data associated to that storage key.
```

So if the messages not be executed successfully due to wrong messages provided by the users or any other reasons, the same `cc_id` can't be executed again because the message status still be `Executed` status.


